    cardEl.appendChild(image);
    var contentDiv = document.querySelector("#page #mid_panel #content");
    contentDiv.appendChild(cardEl);
!}

Although the arch-enemy of democracy had been installed as chancellor, to everyone's surprise, the usual political violence marked that day. The <span style="color: #000000;">rep</span><span style="color: #DD0000;">ubl</span><span style="color: #FFCC00;">ican</span> parties haven't had the expected reaction to his appointment, and many believe that we should bide our time and prepare for a final showdown when [+ royalist_chancellor +] likely violates the constitution. Many also believe that DuFour will keep [+ royalist_chancellor +] in check, and save Commonwealth democracy from destruction.

Most people have no idea what has befallen them; the installation of yet another chancellor had become such a common occurrence that a dangerous amount of ordinary folk have grown indifferent.

This astonishing turnabout in [+ royalist_leader +]'s fortunes confirmed his belief that he was a man of destiny, certain to succeed in his plan to purge the Commonwealth of all who stood against the Crown, and wage endless wars to force the realms back under the Empress, all across Athar. Gallax had not seized power; it had been handed to him by the men who at that moment controlled the Commonwealth’s destiny.

What are we to do now?

- @bide_time
- @civil_war_pre

@bide_time
title: Bide our time, wait until [+ royalist_chancellor +] makes an unconstitutional move first, then strike.

